title: Instructions/get_tiddlers

Batch-read multiple tiddlers in one call. Saves round-trips when you already have a list of titles (e.g. from `run_filter` or `list_tiddlers`).

|!Parameter |!Required |!Description |
|`titles` |yes |Array of tiddler titles; input order preserved |
|`detailed` |no |Include the `text` field (default: `true`) |
|`verbose` |no |Include bookkeeping fields (`created`/`modified`/`creator`/`modifier`/`revision`) (default: `false`) |
|`format` |no |`hashline` (default), `tid`, or `json` |
|`max_tiddlers` |no |Hard cap on tiddler count (default: 50) |
|`max_bytes` |no |Hard cap on total output size (default: 50000); first-to-hit wins |

Output is a CompoundTiddlers stream: one `.tid` block per tiddler, separated by `\n+\n`. Missing titles are listed in a `Missing: ...` trailer.

For the full output format and JSON variant, see [[Bulk Tools]].

''Example prompts:''

* "Read TiddlerA, TiddlerB, and TiddlerC in one call"
* "Fetch the bodies of every tiddler tagged Server"
